#
# Windows 11 10.0.26200 (winoracle, WARP "Microsoft Basic Render Driver"),
# run on the logged-on desktop via schtasks /it (session disconnected, so
# every Present that reaches the screen answers DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED and a
# bitblt Present does not count). 2026-09-28. x86 differs from x64 only in
# FLIP_DISCARD ResizeBuffers(20000x20000): E_OUTOFMEMORY in the 32-bit
# address space.
#
# Rules this measured (implemented in src/winapi/graphics/d3d11/d3d11.cpp):
#  - flip Present: TEST only alone; DO_NOT_SEQUENCE not with RESTART or
#    DO_NOT_WAIT; bits outside DXGI_PRESENT refused. Bitblt ignores them.
#  - creation flags: RESTRICT_SHARED_RESOURCE_DRIVER is E_INVALIDARG on flip,
#    FULLSCREEN_VIDEO / YUV_VIDEO / HW_PROTECTED INVALID_CALL, HOLOGRAPHIC ok.
#  - colour spaces: bitblt sRGB only; 8/10-bit flip adds studio G22 P709,
#    G2084/G22 P2020 and their studio variants; FP16 linear scRGB only.
#  - waitable object: a new handle per call; one frame free at latency 1,
#    raising the latency frees the difference; latency 17 ok, 100 refused.
#  - SetSourceSize(0, h) accepted; ResizeBuffers resets it to the buffer.
#  - a failed bitblt ResizeBuffers (R32_FLOAT) keeps the new description and
#    leaves no buffers: GetBuffer / Present INVALID_CALL until a good resize.
#  - composition SetMatrixTransform: scale/translate only (INVALID_CALL).
#  - a live flip chain refuses a second flip chain on its HWND (ACCESSDENIED);
#    fullscreen desc Windowed=FALSE -> DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED, windowed.
# Vitreo differences that remain: OCCLUDED vs S_OK and bitblt present counts
# (disconnected session), DO_NOT_WAIT answering WAS_STILL_DRAWING when the
# Metal queue is full, 16x MSAA and 20000x20000 (Metal limits: E_INVALIDARG /
# E_OUTOFMEMORY), studio-range colour spaces (no presenter support).
